An error other than an HTTPERROR that escapes a handler responds 500
{"error": "INTERNAL ERROR", "requestId": ...}, and the error itself is not
sent to the client (Requirement 6.5).

### THROW ERROR
GET /flood
=> 500

{"error": "INTERNAL ERROR", "requestId": "<any string>"}

### a runtime error: division by zero
GET /divide
=> 500

{"error": "INTERNAL ERROR", "requestId": "<any string>"}

### a runtime error: a member of NIL
GET /nil
=> 500

{"error": "INTERNAL ERROR", "requestId": "<any string>"}

### the server keeps serving
GET /ok
=> 200

{"ok": true}
